  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given URL missing regardingId, NotepadShell renders MessageBar with error text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Close button attempts window.close; on failure, attempts postMessage; never throws.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo-opened webresources typically respond to window.close(); test in dev environment during task 039 QA.

  ---
  ## Completion notes (2026-07-03)

  Implemented:
  - `NotepadErrorBanner` component in NotepadShell.tsx (Fluent v9 MessageBar + Close button; icon-in-containerAction slot + labeled button); intent="error" for invalid-launch/repo-error, intent="warning" for unsupported entity.
  - `handleNotepadClose()` with two-strategy sequence: window.close() → postMessage({type:"notepad-close"}, "*"). Both wrapped in try/catch (defensive).
  - Three error-state early-returns in NotepadShell now render NotepadErrorBanner instead of placeholder divs. data-testid + data-error-state hooks preserved.
  - Fixed pre-existing jest.config.cjs typo: `setupFilesAfterEach` → `setupFilesAfterEnv` (correct Jest config key; the wrong key silently no-op'd the jest.setup.cjs, which was loading matchMedia + ResizeObserver polyfills). All 102 tests still pass after fix.
  - Notes: `projects/record-header-and-notepad-r1/notes/close-mechanism.md` documenting U-01 resolution.

  Tests: 21 NotepadShell tests (was 16; +5 net new for MessageBar rendering + Close-button behavior). Full Notepad suite: 102/102 (was 97).

  Findings:
  - Fluent v9 MessageBar renders as `role="group"` (not `role="alert"`); tests assert on role="group" to confirm shell mount.
  - `role="alert"` mapping requires MessageBar.politeness="assertive" prop (default is polite → group). Kept default for our error banners since they are already visually prominent and non-transient.
  - MessageBarActions.containerAction slot correctly rendered dismiss icon; click behavior verified separately from the labeled Close button.</notes>

